A||||10||Urchin||Some more guess work...(opinions)||||1||
Z||000000||Urchin||09-13-2001||10:01 PM||||I have been taking all of this in the past couple of days, along with everyone else.  Something just occured to me.  It may be a little on the far side, but I'll say it anyway.  Consider this...  after viewing the "Coup" album cover(which supposedly was preduced prior to the incident), viewing the comments by that psycho on the "Google" message board who appeared to have known something about what was going to happen (his 911 post)(assuming it wasn't a lucky guess)...  I actually attempted to e-mail this guy and realized that his email extension ".moc" is used by the Ministry of Communication for the state of Isreal.  Now he also said in another post that there would be more to come (as some of you may remember).  Now we have all of these terrorists being detained as they try to get back in the air (and rumours are flying about the possibility of a planned second attack).  There are more details that has brought me to this conclusion, but at this point it is not necessary to list them.  Anyhow, what I am considering, is whether it is possible for which ever country (or countries) that is behind this to have kept this knowledge (of the attacks to take place)within its boundaries, meaning that civilians may have been aware before it took place.  How else could all of these people been aware of these events before they happened (assuming they are not a part of the terrorist organization)?   Considering what I have seen, I can't see all of these things being coincidences.  Any comments on this...  is this a little far fetched..?     <P>Just in case you are unsure of who the "psycho" I have refered to is, here again is a link to his most recent post... <A HREF="http://groups.google.com/groups?q=author:tesnal%40psl.moc&hl=en&rnum=1&selm=3b9e9223%40monitor.lanset.com" TARGET=_blank>http://groups.google.com/groups?q=author:tesnal%40psl.moc&hl=en&rnum= 1&selm=3b9e9223%40monitor.lanset.com</A> <BR>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 09-13-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 09-13-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 09-13-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||09-13-2001||11:27 PM||||Urchin: I can guaratee you that people knew that "something big was going to go down." I can state with almost complete certainty that no-one was leaking the actual plans. The "Coup" thing was a coincidnce, no more. It's not the first album cover with explosions on it. Any other time, it might have been funny: Two hommies throwing a party under an exploding building. Any political context you can find in this has probably been created by the viewer. Almost like seeing the devil in the smoke. Of course, now that it's ACTUALLY happened, it's in terrible bad taste...<P>As for leads popping up, 99.9% of them will be bunk. Thing is, that 0.1% of them might have some worth. Anything that helps catch these animals is a Good Thing. The FBI is made up of Really Suspicious Bastards. I'm sure that they are glad that there are people outside the agency just like them harvesting information for them.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000002||Urchin||09-13-2001||11:38 PM||||I see your point, and you are probably right.  Perhaps the details were not known.  I was not necessarily implying that the general public of the countries in question had these details, but simply knew "something".  Which I assume is what you are also stating.  On a bit of a side note, I dug up the definition of "coup" for those who are not aware of the definition.  It is rather interesting, not necessarily implying it means anything, just that it is interesting   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  <A HREF="http://machaut.uchicago.edu/cgi-bin/WEBSTER.sh?WORD=coup" TARGET=_blank>http://machaut.uchicago.edu/cgi-bin/WEBSTER.sh?WORD=coup</A> <BR>Anyway, thanks for your thoughts...  <BR>By the way, my intentions are not to focus on "Coup".  I am interested in hearing opinions on the possibility of the thoughts I listed above and any other thoughts people here may have.<P><BR>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 09-13-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||09-13-2001||11:47 PM||||Well, some friends and I were discussing how we could plan this whole mess online, in an hour or less:<BR>I could almost guarantee that this whole thing was co-ordinated at least partly online...||||reg||3
Z||000004||Tonker||09-14-2001||01:18 AM||||You might be on the right track. I don't think the civilian population had any idea about it, though. It's a bad idea to leak plans when you're trying to accomplish something like this, wouldn't you agree?<P>Of higer probability to me is that someone within the organisation was doing this over the Internet and doesn't think they will be caught. Another option is that an intelligence agency in another country got wind of this somehow and decided not to share the info. Could be arab( Iraqi connection maybe? ), could be Israeli. I mentioned in another thread that it seemed unlikely to me that the Israelis with all of their resources and assets in the region didn't have any clue that something of this magnitude was going down. Maybe they didn't.<P>Let's be honest, it could be just about anything really. We'll have to wait until we get a bit more info on this one.||||reg||5
Z||000005||Mach10||09-14-2001||01:49 AM||||Part of the success of the plan was the sheer improbability of it. One plane? HA! In a million years. Two planes? Impossible. 4 planes? I'd bet that the notion was inconcievable to the people on high. It was well executed. I can only hope that the same goes for the perps. Well Executed.||||reg||13
